# Keep the build context to source.
#
# bin/ and obj/ matter most: they hold this machine's restore output, including absolute paths
# into a NuGet cache the container does not have. Copying them over the container's own restore
# makes the publish fail with NETSDK1064, which reads like a missing package rather than what it
# is — the host's build output shadowing the container's.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/

# Never in an image: local credentials, licence signing keys, and anything the developer's
# environment happens to hold.
secrets/
**/*.private.pem
.env
.git/
.github/
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Nothing the running service reads.
docs/
design/
tests/
**/*.md
